  "content": {
    "id": "p82-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "A farmer has $300$ metres of fencing. A rectangular field is built beside a river, so the river-facing side requires no fence. The farmer also installs one internal dividing fence perpendicular to the river.\n\nLet $x$ be the distance perpendicular to the river and $y$ the length parallel to it.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p82-q13-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that\n$$3x+y=300.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Three fences have length $x$ and one has length $y$, so $3x+y=300$.",
          "worked": "The fencing consists of two outer sides of length $x$, one internal divider of length $x$, and one side of length $y$. Thus\n$$\\begin{align*}x+x+x+y&=300\\\\3x+y&=300.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p82-q13-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Write the area $A$ as a quadratic function of $x$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$A=-3x^2+300x$.",
          "worked": "Since $y=300-3x$, the area is\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=xy\\\\A&=x(300-3x)\\\\A&=-3x^2+300x.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p82-q13-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Write the area function in vertex form.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$A=-3(x-50)^2+7500$.",
          "worked": "Complete the square:\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=-3(x^2-100x)\\\\A&=-3(x^2-100x+2500-2500)\\\\A&=-3\\bigl((x-50)^2-2500\\bigr)\\\\A&=-3(x-50)^2+7500.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p82-q13-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Find the dimensions that maximise the area.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$50\\text{ m}$ perpendicular to the river and $150\\text{ m}$ parallel to it.",
          "worked": "The area parabola is concave down, so its vertex gives the maximum at $x=50$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=300-3(50)\\\\y&=150.\\end{align*}$$\nThe optimal dimensions are $50$ metres perpendicular to the river by $150$ metres parallel to it.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p82-q13-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "Find the maximum area.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$7500\\text{ m}^2$.",
          "worked": "At the vertex,\n$$A_{\\max}=7500\\text{ m}^2.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p82-q13-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "State the relationship between the optimal length and width.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The optimal length is three times the width: $y=3x$.",
          "worked": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p82-q13-root-bank-d80d01c1-c74a-45e0-8465-b35f3e0ddddd",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "At the optimum, ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x=50",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "y=150",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", so",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "break"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "y=150=3(50)=3x.",
                    "display": true
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "break"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The optimal length is three times the width.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      }
    ]
